# The published list of the kinds of a lemma's proof (com.yang_bo.gezi.standardlibrary.LemmaProof): munit, the full name of a
# munit suite that checks the lemma; md, a Markdown link to the document that proves it; tex, a TeX citation; each of
# one field, a trie of a string literal.
# A Scott sum whose constructors are the tuple's fields, in the order of the enum's cases, read by position
# (LemmaProof.ofAlternative). A knowledge file writes a constructor, imported from this file or written closed (the
# two are one term), as the last field of a member of its slot lemmas, and KnowledgeFileReading reads which
# alternative it takes by structure, never by a name: the host reads no string.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λsuite munit md tex. munit suite)
λ munit
. (λtuple. tuple λlink munit md tex. md link)
λ md
. (λtuple. tuple λcitation munit md tex. tex citation)
λ tex
. export munit md tex
